K0.2 logs with no directory MANIFEST: 33
  digest found in K0.2/implementation-*.md and matching the file bytes: 33
  unpinned: 0

CONCLUSION: nothing is unpinned. Revision 6's clause was inverted; revision 7 states
the measured census and the objection that survives it — a digest pins bytes and
certifies no whitespace hygiene, which is why 'they are digest-pinned' was never a
reason a linter could safely skip them.

## The companion clause: does 'hand-authored prose' discriminate?
$ python3   # how many exempted logs open with a "#" header line?
  73 of 458 open with a '#' header line
006's environment rule and this packet's own round-6 remediation REQUIRE an authored
header on every capture, so an authored opening line is the norm the process asks for,
not a symptom. The clause is corrected in revision 7 rather than repeated.

## Boundary instability — the argument the measurements strengthen
  A: 433
  C7: 453
  H7a: 458
  The exempted set widens every round. A carve-out with no stable boundary is the
  durable objection; it does not depend on the pinning claim at all.
